I'm not sure this fix restores the original behavior of the code prior to #50511.

It used to be:
```cpp
for (List<PropertyInfo>::Element *E = local.front(); E; E = E->next()) {
		PropertyInfo pi = E->get();
		pi.name = "shader_param/" + pi.name;
		params_cache[pi.name] = E->get().name;
```
i.e. `pi` was a copy which got its named modified.

With the new code, `pi` is a reference, so we're modifying the name of `local`'s copy of the param list IINM.

I don't know if it's a problem, but that's worth noting.

Later on we pass `pi` to `p_params` while it was owned by `local`... my Rust beginner brain wonders what the C++ missing borrow checker thinks about that :D
